---
title: "Search"
description: "Search all posts on Vojtech Ruzicka's Programming Blog."
permalink: /search/
bodyClass: search-page
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{#
  Dedicated search page, the target of the homepage `SearchAction` JSON-LD
  (`/search/?q={query}`): the query from the URL is run automatically and the
  URL is kept in sync while typing, so a search can be linked to or bookmarked.
  Unlike the other layouts, <main> deliberately carries no `data-pagefind-body`,
  which keeps this page out of the Pagefind index (see pagefind.yaml).
  Results render inline (`data-search-inline`) instead of in the header overlay.
#}
{% block content %}
  <main id="content" class="page content">
    <header>
      {% include "components/breadcrumbs.njk" %}
      <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="js-pagefind search-page-ui" id="search-page" data-search-inline>
      <!-- Placeholder only: replaced by Pagefind UI as soon as the script loads -->
      <div class="pagefind-ui">
        <form class="pagefind-ui__form" role="search" aria-label="Search the site">
          <input class="pagefind-ui__search-input" type="text" name="q" placeholder="Search…" title="Search the site"
                 aria-label="Search" autocapitalize="none" enterkeyhint="search" data-1p-ignore />
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>

    <noscript>
      <p>Search needs JavaScript. Without it, browse the posts by <a href="/topics/">topic</a> instead.</p>
    </noscript>
  </main>
{% endblock %}
